WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.380
Two-handed pinochle, start to finish,
in one hand.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.997
You and the computer, Dix,
each hold twelve cards.

00:00:12.997 --> 00:00:17.193
You score two ways: by laying down melds,
which are card combinations,

00:00:17.193 --> 00:00:21.030
and by winning tricks that hold
aces, tens, and kings.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.214
The card turned up under the stock
sets trump for this deal.

00:00:26.214 --> 00:00:30.680
Here, it's clubs. Any trump beats
every card of the other three suits.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.998
Cards rank ace, ten, king,
queen, jack, nine.

00:00:39.998 --> 00:00:41.863
Yes, the ten beats the king.

00:00:41.863 --> 00:00:46.860
To win a trick, play a higher card
of the same suit, or any trump.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.130
Cards you capture score points.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:57.558
An ace is eleven, a ten is ten, a king four,
a queen three, and a jack two.

00:00:57.558 --> 00:01:02.290
After each trick, both players draw a card,
and the winner leads next.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.985
Win a trick, and you may
lay down one meld.

00:01:06.985 --> 00:01:10.914
A king and queen of trump make
a royal marriage, worth forty points.

00:01:10.914 --> 00:01:13.710
Melded cards stay yours to play later.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:33.414
Dix melded too.

00:01:33.414 --> 00:01:38.220
Its meld lies face up, so now you know
some of the cards in its hand.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.857
When the stock runs out,
the playoff begins.

00:02:19.857 --> 00:02:23.320
Your melds go back in your hand,
and now you must follow suit.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.930
If you can't, you must play a trump.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.171
That's a deal. Your score is your melds
plus your trick points.

00:03:04.171 --> 00:03:08.410
In the full game, deals continue
until someone reaches one thousand.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:20.600
Pinochle: Two-Handed.
Free to try on the App Store.
